    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 1.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf, p.125",
      "values:originalText": "For the purpose of this Convention the term “discrimination”\nincludes—\n(a) any distinction, exclusion or preference made on the basis of race,\ncolour, sex, religion, political opinion, national extraction or social\norigin, which has the effect of nullifying or impairing equality of\nopportunity or treatment in employment or occupation;\n\nSchedule 1  Convention concerning Discrimination in respect of Employment and\nOccupation\n\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) such other distinction, exclusion or preference which has the effect of\nnullifying or impairing equality of opportunity or treatment in\nemployment or occupation as may be determined by the Member\nconcerned after consultation with representative employer’s and\nworker’s organisations, where such exist, and with other appropriate\nbodies.\n2.\nAny distinction, exclusion or preference in respect of a particular job\nbased on the inherent requirements thereof shall not be deemed to be\ndiscrimination.\n3.\nFor the purpose of this Convention the terms “employment” and\n“occupation” include access to vocational training, access to employment and to\nparticular occupations, and terms and conditions of employment.",
      "skos:definition": "For the purpose of this Convention the term “discrimination”\nincludes—\n(a) any distinction, exclusion or preference made on the basis of race,\ncolour, sex, religion, political opinion, national extraction or social\norigin, which has the effect of nullifying or impairing equality of\nopportunity or treatment in employment or occupation;\n\nSchedule 1  Convention concerning Discrimination in respect of Employment and\nOccupation\n\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) such other distinction, exclusion or preference which has the effect of\nnullifying or impairing equality of opportunity or treatment in\nemployment or occupation as may be determined by the Member\nconcerned after consultation with representative employer’s and\nworker’s organisations, where such exist, and with other appropriate\nbodies.\n2.\nAny distinction, exclusion or preference in respect of a particular job\nbased on the inherent requirements thereof shall not be deemed to be\ndiscrimination.\n3.\nFor the purpose of this Convention the terms “employment” and\n“occupation” include access to vocational training, access to employment and to\nparticular occupations, and terms and conditions of employment.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-1-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "af675236a5049ee18b8f462238d4e23da6becf0fcd229b2cf410a152ea238437",
      "skos:note": "Discrimination includes distinctions, exclusions or preferences affecting equality of opportunity or treatment in employment or occupation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 1.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 125,
      "values:originalText": "For the purpose of this Convention the term “discrimination”\nincludes—\n(a) any distinction, exclusion or preference made on the basis of race,\ncolour, sex, religion, political opinion, national extraction or social\norigin, which has the effect of nullifying or impairing equality of\nopportunity or treatment in employment or occupation;\n\nSchedule 1  Convention concerning Discrimination in respect of Employment and\nOccupation\n\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) such other distinction, exclusion or preference which has the effect of\nnullifying or impairing equality of opportunity or treatment in\nemployment or occupation as may be determined by the Member\nconcerned after consultation with representative employer’s and\nworker’s organisations, where such exist, and with other appropriate\nbodies.\n2.\nAny distinction, exclusion or preference in respect of a particular job\nbased on the inherent requirements thereof shall not be deemed to be\ndiscrimination.\n3.\nFor the purpose of this Convention the terms “employment” and\n“occupation” include access to vocational training, access to employment and to\nparticular occupations, and terms and conditions of employment."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-1"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
