      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2 Each Member for which this Convention is in force undertakes to declare",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf, p.126",
      "values:originalText": "and pursue a national policy designed to promote, by methods appropriate to\nnational conditions and practice, equality of opportunity and treatment in\nrespect of employment and occupation, with a view to eliminating any\ndiscrimination in respect thereof.",
      "skos:definition": "and pursue a national policy designed to promote, by methods appropriate to\nnational conditions and practice, equality of opportunity and treatment in\nrespect of employment and occupation, with a view to eliminating any\ndiscrimination in respect thereof.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a2f7a3fe5e327d621f87fd7d4b18310f8efabbbcd1c8cb51ff818f8b25f2d6ea",
      "skos:note": "Member undertakes to declare and pursue a national policy promoting equality of opportunity and treatment in employment and occupation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 Each Member for which this Convention is in force undertakes to declare",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 126,
      "values:originalText": "and pursue a national policy designed to promote, by methods appropriate to\nnational conditions and practice, equality of opportunity and treatment in\nrespect of employment and occupation, with a view to eliminating any\ndiscrimination in respect thereof."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "undertaking",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Member undertakes to perform an action.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 Each Member for which this Convention is in force undertakes, by",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf, p.126",
      "values:originalText": "methods appropriate to national conditions and practice—\n(a) to seek the co-operation of employers’ and workers’ organisations and\nother appropriate bodies in promoting the acceptance and observance of\nthis policy;\n(b) to enact such legislation and to promote such educational programmes\nas may be calculated to secure the acceptance and observance of the\npolicy;\n(c) to repeal any statutory provisions and modify any administrative\ninstructions or practices which are inconsistent with the policy;\n(d) to pursue the policy in respect of employment under the direct control\nof a national authority;\n(e) to ensure observance of the policy in the activities of vocational\nguidance, vocational training and placement services under the direction\nof a national authority;\n\nConvention concerning Discrimination in respect of Employment and Occupation\nSchedule 1\n\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(f) to indicate in its annual reports on the application of the Convention the\naction taken in pursuance of the policy and the results secured by such\naction.",
      "skos:definition": "methods appropriate to national conditions and practice—\n(a) to seek the co-operation of employers’ and workers’ organisations and\nother appropriate bodies in promoting the acceptance and observance of\nthis policy;\n(b) to enact such legislation and to promote such educational programmes\nas may be calculated to secure the acceptance and observance of the\npolicy;\n(c) to repeal any statutory provisions and modify any administrative\ninstructions or practices which are inconsistent with the policy;\n(d) to pursue the policy in respect of employment under the direct control\nof a national authority;\n(e) to ensure observance of the policy in the activities of vocational\nguidance, vocational training and placement services under the direction\nof a national authority;\n\nConvention concerning Discrimination in respect of Employment and Occupation\nSchedule 1\n\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(f) to indicate in its annual reports on the application of the Convention the\naction taken in pursuance of the policy and the results secured by such\naction.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5e3d84e15d21662aa540cbaf413df281a4b6a90668f851e22b950fb47ad6498e",
      "skos:note": "Each Member undertakes to seek co-operation, enact legislation, and promote educational programmes."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3 Each Member for which this Convention is in force undertakes, by",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 126,
      "values:originalText": "methods appropriate to national conditions and practice—\n(a) to seek the co-operation of employers’ and workers’ organisations and\nother appropriate bodies in promoting the acceptance and observance of\nthis policy;\n(b) to enact such legislation and to promote such educational programmes\nas may be calculated to secure the acceptance and observance of the\npolicy;\n(c) to repeal any statutory provisions and modify any administrative\ninstructions or practices which are inconsistent with the policy;\n(d) to pursue the policy in respect of employment under the direct control\nof a national authority;\n(e) to ensure observance of the policy in the activities of vocational\nguidance, vocational training and placement services under the direction\nof a national authority;\n\nConvention concerning Discrimination in respect of Employment and Occupation\nSchedule 1\n\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(f) to indicate in its annual reports on the application of the Convention the\naction taken in pursuance of the policy and the results secured by such\naction."
    },
