    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-13",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "13 1.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-13"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf, p.129",
      "values:originalText": "Should the Conference adopt a new Convention revising this\nConvention in whole or in part, then, unless the new Convention otherwise\nprovides—\n(a)\nthe ratification by a Member of the new revising Convention shall\nipso jure involve the immediate denunciation of this Convention,\nnotwithstanding the provisions of Article 9 above, if and when the\nnew revising Convention shall have come into force;\n(b)\nas from the date when the new revising Convention comes into force\nthis Convention shall cease to be open to ratification by the Members.\n2.\nThis Convention shall in any case remain in force in its actual form\nand content for those Members which have ratified it but have not ratified the\nrevising Convention.",
      "skos:definition": "Should the Conference adopt a new Convention revising this\nConvention in whole or in part, then, unless the new Convention otherwise\nprovides—\n(a)\nthe ratification by a Member of the new revising Convention shall\nipso jure involve the immediate denunciation of this Convention,\nnotwithstanding the provisions of Article 9 above, if and when the\nnew revising Convention shall have come into force;\n(b)\nas from the date when the new revising Convention comes into force\nthis Convention shall cease to be open to ratification by the Members.\n2.\nThis Convention shall in any case remain in force in its actual form\nand content for those Members which have ratified it but have not ratified the\nrevising Convention.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-13-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-13-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "84c36352cbe65fadfe7d5237ff1564f71a598fe8af912593fabd151530363945",
      "skos:note": "Denunciation of Convention upon new revising Convention coming into force"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-13",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "13 1.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 129,
      "values:originalText": "Should the Conference adopt a new Convention revising this\nConvention in whole or in part, then, unless the new Convention otherwise\nprovides—\n(a)\nthe ratification by a Member of the new revising Convention shall\nipso jure involve the immediate denunciation of this Convention,\nnotwithstanding the provisions of Article 9 above, if and when the\nnew revising Convention shall have come into force;\n(b)\nas from the date when the new revising Convention comes into force\nthis Convention shall cease to be open to ratification by the Members.\n2.\nThis Convention shall in any case remain in force in its actual form\nand content for those Members which have ratified it but have not ratified the\nrevising Convention."
    },
    {
