      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-1-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 1.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-1-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf, p.130",
      "values:originalText": "All peoples have the right of self-determination. By virtue of that right\nthey freely determine their political status and freely pursue their economic,\nsocial and cultural development.\n2.\nAll peoples may, for their own ends, freely dispose of their natural\nwealth and resources without prejudice to any obligations arising out of\n\nInternational Covenant on Civil and Political Rights  Schedule 2\n\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\ninternational economic co-operation, based upon the principle of mutual benefit,\nand international law. In no case may a people be deprived of its own means of\nsubsistence.\n3.\nThe States Parties to the present Covenant, including those having\nresponsibility for the administration of Non-Self-Governing and Trust\nTerritories, shall promote the realization of the right of self-determination, and\nshall respect that right, in conformity with the provisions of the Charter of the\nUnited Nations.",
      "skos:definition": "All peoples have the right of self-determination. By virtue of that right\nthey freely determine their political status and freely pursue their economic,\nsocial and cultural development.\n2.\nAll peoples may, for their own ends, freely dispose of their natural\nwealth and resources without prejudice to any obligations arising out of\n\nInternational Covenant on Civil and Political Rights  Schedule 2\n\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\ninternational economic co-operation, based upon the principle of mutual benefit,\nand international law. In no case may a people be deprived of its own means of\nsubsistence.\n3.\nThe States Parties to the present Covenant, including those having\nresponsibility for the administration of Non-Self-Governing and Trust\nTerritories, shall promote the realization of the right of self-determination, and\nshall respect that right, in conformity with the provisions of the Charter of the\nUnited Nations.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-1-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-1-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-1-2-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ca0dd3c2ea905b5bf1e535c0cc5a8917ff0168e2cdd6d8280ae1ee425c6e2e7b",
      "skos:note": "Right of self-determination"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-1-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 1.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 130,
      "values:originalText": "All peoples have the right of self-determination. By virtue of that right\nthey freely determine their political status and freely pursue their economic,\nsocial and cultural development.\n2.\nAll peoples may, for their own ends, freely dispose of their natural\nwealth and resources without prejudice to any obligations arising out of\n\nInternational Covenant on Civil and Political Rights  Schedule 2\n\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\ninternational economic co-operation, based upon the principle of mutual benefit,\nand international law. In no case may a people be deprived of its own means of\nsubsistence.\n3.\nThe States Parties to the present Covenant, including those having\nresponsibility for the administration of Non-Self-Governing and Trust\nTerritories, shall promote the realization of the right of self-determination, and\nshall respect that right, in conformity with the provisions of the Charter of the\nUnited Nations."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-1-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Right",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-1-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:heldBy": {
        "@id": "values:NaturalPerson"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-1-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "hasRight",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Right of self-determination",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "All peoples have the right of self-determination."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-1-2-logic-descriptionlogic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "subClassOf",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Subclass of human rights",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Right of self-determination is a fundamental human right."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-2-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2 1.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-2-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf, p.131",
      "values:originalText": "Each State Party to the present Covenant undertakes to respect and to\nensure to all individuals within its territory and subject to its jurisdiction the\nrights recognized in the present Covenant, without distinction of any kind, such\nas race, colour, sex, language, religion, political or other opinion, national or\nsocial origin, property, birth or other status.\n2.\nWhere not already provided for by existing legislative or other\nmeasures, each State Party to the present Covenant undertakes to take the\nnecessary steps, in accordance with its constitutional processes and with the\nprovisions of the present Covenant, to adopt such legislative or other measures\nas may be necessary to give effect to the rights recognized in the present\nCovenant.\n3.\nEach State Party to the present Covenant undertakes:\n(a) To ensure that any person whose rights or freedoms as herein\nrecognized are violated shall have an effective remedy, notwithstanding that the\nviolation has been committed by persons acting in an official capacity;\n(b) To ensure that any person claiming such a remedy shall have his right\nthereto determined by competent judicial, administrative or legislative\nauthorities, or by any other competent authority provided for by the legal\nsystem of the State, and to develop the possibilities of judicial remedy;\n(c) To ensure that the competent authorities shall enforce such remedies\nwhen granted.",
      "skos:definition": "Each State Party to the present Covenant undertakes to respect and to\nensure to all individuals within its territory and subject to its jurisdiction the\nrights recognized in the present Covenant, without distinction of any kind, such\nas race, colour, sex, language, religion, political or other opinion, national or\nsocial origin, property, birth or other status.\n2.\nWhere not already provided for by existing legislative or other\nmeasures, each State Party to the present Covenant undertakes to take the\nnecessary steps, in accordance with its constitutional processes and with the\nprovisions of the present Covenant, to adopt such legislative or other measures\nas may be necessary to give effect to the rights recognized in the present\nCovenant.\n3.\nEach State Party to the present Covenant undertakes:\n(a) To ensure that any person whose rights or freedoms as herein\nrecognized are violated shall have an effective remedy, notwithstanding that the\nviolation has been committed by persons acting in an official capacity;\n(b) To ensure that any person claiming such a remedy shall have his right\nthereto determined by competent judicial, administrative or legislative\nauthorities, or by any other competent authority provided for by the legal\nsystem of the State, and to develop the possibilities of judicial remedy;\n(c) To ensure that the competent authorities shall enforce such remedies\nwhen granted.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-2-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-2-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "21d029905c88507db3a95c216f30e6eab3cb4f27d0d99dd2bdb186ccb424c82b",
      "skos:note": "Each State Party undertakes to respect and ensure rights for individuals within its territory."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-2-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 1.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 131,
      "values:originalText": "Each State Party to the present Covenant undertakes to respect and to\nensure to all individuals within its territory and subject to its jurisdiction the\nrights recognized in the present Covenant, without distinction of any kind, such\nas race, colour, sex, language, religion, political or other opinion, national or\nsocial origin, property, birth or other status.\n2.\nWhere not already provided for by existing legislative or other\nmeasures, each State Party to the present Covenant undertakes to take the\nnecessary steps, in accordance with its constitutional processes and with the\nprovisions of the present Covenant, to adopt such legislative or other measures\nas may be necessary to give effect to the rights recognized in the present\nCovenant.\n3.\nEach State Party to the present Covenant undertakes:\n(a) To ensure that any person whose rights or freedoms as herein\nrecognized are violated shall have an effective remedy, notwithstanding that the\nviolation has been committed by persons acting in an official capacity;\n(b) To ensure that any person claiming such a remedy shall have his right\nthereto determined by competent judicial, administrative or legislative\nauthorities, or by any other competent authority provided for by the legal\nsystem of the State, and to develop the possibilities of judicial remedy;\n(c) To ensure that the competent authorities shall enforce such remedies\nwhen granted."
    },
