      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Public emergency threatens life of nation",
      "cml:conclusionText": "State may take measures"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-5-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 1.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-5-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf, p.132",
      "values:originalText": "Nothing in the present Covenant may be interpreted as implying for\nany State, group or person any right to engage in any activity or perform any act\naimed at the destruction of any of the rights and freedoms recognized herein or\nat their limitation to a greater extent than is provided for in the present\nCovenant.\n2.\nThere shall be no restriction upon or derogation from any of the\nfundamental human rights recognized or existing in any State Party to the\npresent Covenant pursuant to law, conventions, regulations or custom on the\npretext that the present Covenant does not recognize such rights or that it\nrecognizes them to a lesser extent.\n\nInternational Covenant on Civil and Political Rights  Schedule 2\n\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "Nothing in the present Covenant may be interpreted as implying for\nany State, group or person any right to engage in any activity or perform any act\naimed at the destruction of any of the rights and freedoms recognized herein or\nat their limitation to a greater extent than is provided for in the present\nCovenant.\n2.\nThere shall be no restriction upon or derogation from any of the\nfundamental human rights recognized or existing in any State Party to the\npresent Covenant pursuant to law, conventions, regulations or custom on the\npretext that the present Covenant does not recognize such rights or that it\nrecognizes them to a lesser extent.\n\nInternational Covenant on Civil and Political Rights  Schedule 2\n\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-5-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-5-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-5-2-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-5-2-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-5-2-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d2f9e85b77a2543f6b0610a6ec6e8cd3d46e3f871877ad1a017583d2c79b9f9a",
      "skos:note": "No right to engage in activity aimed at destruction of rights and freedoms"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-5-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 1.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 132,
      "values:originalText": "Nothing in the present Covenant may be interpreted as implying for\nany State, group or person any right to engage in any activity or perform any act\naimed at the destruction of any of the rights and freedoms recognized herein or\nat their limitation to a greater extent than is provided for in the present\nCovenant.\n2.\nThere shall be no restriction upon or derogation from any of the\nfundamental human rights recognized or existing in any State Party to the\npresent Covenant pursuant to law, conventions, regulations or custom on the\npretext that the present Covenant does not recognize such rights or that it\nrecognizes them to a lesser extent.\n\nInternational Covenant on Civil and Political Rights  Schedule 2\n\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
