      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Nothing in the present Covenant may be interpreted as implying...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...aimed at the destruction of any of the rights and freedoms recognized herein or..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-5-2-logic-alleninterval-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "TemporalOverlap",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Overlaps with existing laws, regulations, conventions, and custom",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "There shall be no restriction upon or derogation from...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...pursuant to law, conventions, regulations or custom on the pretext that the present Covenant does not recognize such rights or that it recognizes them to a lesser extent."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-5-2-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "States obligation to respect fundamental human rights",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "There shall be no restriction upon or derogation from...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...fundamental human rights recognized or existing in any State Party to the present Covenant pursuant to law, conventions, regulations or custom..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-6-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6 1.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-6-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf, p.133",
      "values:originalText": "Every human being has the inherent right to life. This right shall be\nprotected by law. No one shall be arbitrarily deprived of his life.\n2.\nIn countries which have not abolished the death penalty, sentence of\ndeath may be imposed only for the most serious crimes in accordance with the\nlaw in force at the time of the commission of the crime and not contrary to the\nprovisions of the present Covenant and to the Convention on the Prevention and\nPunishment of the Crime of Genocide. This penalty can only be carried out\npursuant to a final judgment rendered by a competent court.\n3.\nWhen deprivation of life constitutes the crime of genocide, it is\nunderstood that nothing in this article shall authorize any State Party to the\npresent Covenant to derogate in any way from any obligation assumed under the\nprovisions of the Convention on the Prevention and Punishment of the Crime of\nGenocide.\n4.\nAnyone sentenced to death shall have the right to seek pardon or\ncommutation of the sentence. Amnesty, pardon or commutation of the sentence\nof death may be granted in all cases.\n5.\nSentence of death shall not be imposed for crimes committed by\npersons below eighteen years of age and shall not be carried out on pregnant\nwomen.\n6.\nNothing in this article shall be invoked to delay or to prevent the\nabolition of capital punishment by any State Party to the present Covenant.",
      "skos:definition": "Every human being has the inherent right to life. This right shall be\nprotected by law. No one shall be arbitrarily deprived of his life.\n2.\nIn countries which have not abolished the death penalty, sentence of\ndeath may be imposed only for the most serious crimes in accordance with the\nlaw in force at the time of the commission of the crime and not contrary to the\nprovisions of the present Covenant and to the Convention on the Prevention and\nPunishment of the Crime of Genocide. This penalty can only be carried out\npursuant to a final judgment rendered by a competent court.\n3.\nWhen deprivation of life constitutes the crime of genocide, it is\nunderstood that nothing in this article shall authorize any State Party to the\npresent Covenant to derogate in any way from any obligation assumed under the\nprovisions of the Convention on the Prevention and Punishment of the Crime of\nGenocide.\n4.\nAnyone sentenced to death shall have the right to seek pardon or\ncommutation of the sentence. Amnesty, pardon or commutation of the sentence\nof death may be granted in all cases.\n5.\nSentence of death shall not be imposed for crimes committed by\npersons below eighteen years of age and shall not be carried out on pregnant\nwomen.\n6.\nNothing in this article shall be invoked to delay or to prevent the\nabolition of capital punishment by any State Party to the present Covenant.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-6-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-6-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "96aff714613733f8491e33ccca6c1ec6474cb4c3eba74e808494cbff3d0f988f",
      "skos:note": "Inherent right to life, protection by law, and prohibition on arbitrary deprivation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-6-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6 1.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 133,
      "values:originalText": "Every human being has the inherent right to life. This right shall be\nprotected by law. No one shall be arbitrarily deprived of his life.\n2.\nIn countries which have not abolished the death penalty, sentence of\ndeath may be imposed only for the most serious crimes in accordance with the\nlaw in force at the time of the commission of the crime and not contrary to the\nprovisions of the present Covenant and to the Convention on the Prevention and\nPunishment of the Crime of Genocide. This penalty can only be carried out\npursuant to a final judgment rendered by a competent court.\n3.\nWhen deprivation of life constitutes the crime of genocide, it is\nunderstood that nothing in this article shall authorize any State Party to the\npresent Covenant to derogate in any way from any obligation assumed under the\nprovisions of the Convention on the Prevention and Punishment of the Crime of\nGenocide.\n4.\nAnyone sentenced to death shall have the right to seek pardon or\ncommutation of the sentence. Amnesty, pardon or commutation of the sentence\nof death may be granted in all cases.\n5.\nSentence of death shall not be imposed for crimes committed by\npersons below eighteen years of age and shall not be carried out on pregnant\nwomen.\n6.\nNothing in this article shall be invoked to delay or to prevent the\nabolition of capital punishment by any State Party to the present Covenant."
    },
