      },
      "cml:premiseText": "No one shall be subjected to medical or scientific experimentation without his free consent.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "It is prohibited to subject anyone to medical or scientific experimentation without their consent."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-8-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8 1.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-8-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf, p.133",
      "values:originalText": "No one shall be held in slavery; slavery and the slave-trade in all their\nforms shall be prohibited.\n2.\nNo one shall be held in servitude.\n\nSchedule 2  International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights\n\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n3. (a)\nNo one shall be required to perform forced or compulsory\nlabour;\n(b) Paragraph 3(a) shall not be held to preclude, in countries where\nimprisonment with hard labour may be imposed as a punishment for a crime,\nthe performance of hard labour in pursuance of a sentence to such punishment\nby a competent court;\n(c) For the purpose of this paragraph the term “forced or compulsory\nlabour” shall not include:\n\n(i) Any work or service, not referred to in sub-paragraph (b),\nnormally required of a person who is under detention in\nconsequence of a lawful order of a court, or of a person during\nconditional release from such detention;\n\n(ii) Any service of a military character and, in countries where\nconscientious objection is recognized, any national service\nrequired by law of conscientious objectors;\n\n(iii) Any service exacted in cases of emergency or calamity\nthreatening the life or well-being of the community;\n\n(iv) Any work or service which forms part of normal civil obligations.",
      "skos:definition": "No one shall be held in slavery; slavery and the slave-trade in all their\nforms shall be prohibited.\n2.\nNo one shall be held in servitude.\n\nSchedule 2  International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights\n\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n3. (a)\nNo one shall be required to perform forced or compulsory\nlabour;\n(b) Paragraph 3(a) shall not be held to preclude, in countries where\nimprisonment with hard labour may be imposed as a punishment for a crime,\nthe performance of hard labour in pursuance of a sentence to such punishment\nby a competent court;\n(c) For the purpose of this paragraph the term “forced or compulsory\nlabour” shall not include:\n\n(i) Any work or service, not referred to in sub-paragraph (b),\nnormally required of a person who is under detention in\nconsequence of a lawful order of a court, or of a person during\nconditional release from such detention;\n\n(ii) Any service of a military character and, in countries where\nconscientious objection is recognized, any national service\nrequired by law of conscientious objectors;\n\n(iii) Any service exacted in cases of emergency or calamity\nthreatening the life or well-being of the community;\n\n(iv) Any work or service which forms part of normal civil obligations.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-8-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-8-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ed3e783102fcbba59bac257a12c2392b62ab9df0eadb6cfc9d11bebf87002095",
      "skos:note": "No one shall be held in slavery or servitude."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-8-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8 1.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 133,
      "values:originalText": "No one shall be held in slavery; slavery and the slave-trade in all their\nforms shall be prohibited.\n2.\nNo one shall be held in servitude.\n\nSchedule 2  International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights\n\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n3. (a)\nNo one shall be required to perform forced or compulsory\nlabour;\n(b) Paragraph 3(a) shall not be held to preclude, in countries where\nimprisonment with hard labour may be imposed as a punishment for a crime,\nthe performance of hard labour in pursuance of a sentence to such punishment\nby a competent court;\n(c) For the purpose of this paragraph the term “forced or compulsory\nlabour” shall not include:\n\n(i) Any work or service, not referred to in sub-paragraph (b),\nnormally required of a person who is under detention in\nconsequence of a lawful order of a court, or of a person during\nconditional release from such detention;\n\n(ii) Any service of a military character and, in countries where\nconscientious objection is recognized, any national service\nrequired by law of conscientious objectors;\n\n(iii) Any service exacted in cases of emergency or calamity\nthreatening the life or well-being of the community;\n\n(iv) Any work or service which forms part of normal civil obligations."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-8-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-8-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-8-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits slavery and servitude.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-9-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9 1.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-9-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf, p.134",
      "values:originalText": "Everyone has the right to liberty and security of person. No one shall\nbe subjected to arbitrary arrest or detention. No one shall be deprived of his\nliberty except on such grounds and in accordance with such procedure as are\nestablished by law.\n2.\nAnyone who is arrested shall be informed, at the time of arrest, of the\nreasons for his arrest and shall be promptly informed of any charges against\nhim.\n3.\nAnyone arrested or detained on a criminal charge shall be brought\npromptly before a judge or other officer authorized by law to exercise judicial\npower and shall be entitled to trial within a reasonable time or to release. It shall\nnot be the general rule that persons awaiting trial shall be detained in custody,\nbut release may be subject to guarantees to appear for trial, at any other stage of\nthe judicial proceedings, and, should occasion arise, for execution of the\njudgment.\n4.\nAnyone who is deprived of his liberty by arrest or detention shall be\nentitled to take proceedings before a court, in order that that court may decide\n\nInternational Covenant on Civil and Political Rights  Schedule 2\n\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nwithout delay on the lawfulness of his detention and order his release if the\ndetention is not lawful.\n5.\nAnyone who has been the victim of unlawful arrest or detention shall\nhave an enforceable right to compensation.",
      "skos:definition": "Everyone has the right to liberty and security of person. No one shall\nbe subjected to arbitrary arrest or detention. No one shall be deprived of his\nliberty except on such grounds and in accordance with such procedure as are\nestablished by law.\n2.\nAnyone who is arrested shall be informed, at the time of arrest, of the\nreasons for his arrest and shall be promptly informed of any charges against\nhim.\n3.\nAnyone arrested or detained on a criminal charge shall be brought\npromptly before a judge or other officer authorized by law to exercise judicial\npower and shall be entitled to trial within a reasonable time or to release. It shall\nnot be the general rule that persons awaiting trial shall be detained in custody,\nbut release may be subject to guarantees to appear for trial, at any other stage of\nthe judicial proceedings, and, should occasion arise, for execution of the\njudgment.\n4.\nAnyone who is deprived of his liberty by arrest or detention shall be\nentitled to take proceedings before a court, in order that that court may decide\n\nInternational Covenant on Civil and Political Rights  Schedule 2\n\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nwithout delay on the lawfulness of his detention and order his release if the\ndetention is not lawful.\n5.\nAnyone who has been the victim of unlawful arrest or detention shall\nhave an enforceable right to compensation.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-9-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-9-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c8b13c188dac5c94039b0eb8457664cb1d35d324d9fb5ee5a7d7ee03dc7cf224",
      "skos:note": "Right to liberty and security of person, no arbitrary arrest or detention."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-9-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9 1.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 134,
      "values:originalText": "Everyone has the right to liberty and security of person. No one shall\nbe subjected to arbitrary arrest or detention. No one shall be deprived of his\nliberty except on such grounds and in accordance with such procedure as are\nestablished by law.\n2.\nAnyone who is arrested shall be informed, at the time of arrest, of the\nreasons for his arrest and shall be promptly informed of any charges against\nhim.\n3.\nAnyone arrested or detained on a criminal charge shall be brought\npromptly before a judge or other officer authorized by law to exercise judicial\npower and shall be entitled to trial within a reasonable time or to release. It shall\nnot be the general rule that persons awaiting trial shall be detained in custody,\nbut release may be subject to guarantees to appear for trial, at any other stage of\nthe judicial proceedings, and, should occasion arise, for execution of the\njudgment.\n4.\nAnyone who is deprived of his liberty by arrest or detention shall be\nentitled to take proceedings before a court, in order that that court may decide\n\nInternational Covenant on Civil and Political Rights  Schedule 2\n\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nwithout delay on the lawfulness of his detention and order his release if the\ndetention is not lawful.\n5.\nAnyone who has been the victim of unlawful arrest or detention shall\nhave an enforceable right to compensation."
    },
