    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-10-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 1.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-10-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf, p.135",
      "values:originalText": "All persons deprived of their liberty shall be treated with humanity\nand with respect for the inherent dignity of the human person.\n2. (a)\nAccused persons shall, save in exceptional circumstances, be\nsegregated from convicted persons and shall be subject to separate treatment\nappropriate to their status as unconvicted persons;\n(b) Accused juvenile persons shall be separated from adults and brought\nas speedily as possible for adjudication.\n3.\nThe penitentiary system shall comprise treatment of prisoners the\nessential aim of which shall be their reformation and social rehabilitation.\nJuvenile offenders shall be segregated from adults and be accorded treatment\nappropriate to their age and legal status.",
      "skos:definition": "All persons deprived of their liberty shall be treated with humanity\nand with respect for the inherent dignity of the human person.\n2. (a)\nAccused persons shall, save in exceptional circumstances, be\nsegregated from convicted persons and shall be subject to separate treatment\nappropriate to their status as unconvicted persons;\n(b) Accused juvenile persons shall be separated from adults and brought\nas speedily as possible for adjudication.\n3.\nThe penitentiary system shall comprise treatment of prisoners the\nessential aim of which shall be their reformation and social rehabilitation.\nJuvenile offenders shall be segregated from adults and be accorded treatment\nappropriate to their age and legal status.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-10-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-10-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cd52556c1815516b77bbefddccc1e31da913aea397840f8439aaab68a5e35825",
      "skos:note": "Treat persons deprived of liberty with humanity and respect for human dignity."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-10-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 1.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 135,
      "values:originalText": "All persons deprived of their liberty shall be treated with humanity\nand with respect for the inherent dignity of the human person.\n2. (a)\nAccused persons shall, save in exceptional circumstances, be\nsegregated from convicted persons and shall be subject to separate treatment\nappropriate to their status as unconvicted persons;\n(b) Accused juvenile persons shall be separated from adults and brought\nas speedily as possible for adjudication.\n3.\nThe penitentiary system shall comprise treatment of prisoners the\nessential aim of which shall be their reformation and social rehabilitation.\nJuvenile offenders shall be segregated from adults and be accorded treatment\nappropriate to their age and legal status."
    },
