    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-19",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19 1.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-19"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf, p.138",
      "values:originalText": "Everyone shall have the right to hold opinions without interference.\n2.\nEveryone shall have the right to freedom of expression; this right shall\ninclude freedom to seek, receive and impart information and ideas of all kinds,\nregardless of frontiers, either orally, in writing or in print, in the form of art, or\nthrough any other media of his choice.\n3.\nThe exercise of the rights provided for in paragraph 2 of this article\ncarries with it special duties and responsibilities. It may therefore be subject to\n\nInternational Covenant on Civil and Political Rights  Schedule 2\n\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\ncertain restrictions, but these shall only be such as are provided by law and are\nnecessary:\n(a) For respect of the rights or reputations of others;\n(b) For the protection of national security or of public order (ordre\npublic), or of public health or morals.",
      "skos:definition": "Everyone shall have the right to hold opinions without interference.\n2.\nEveryone shall have the right to freedom of expression; this right shall\ninclude freedom to seek, receive and impart information and ideas of all kinds,\nregardless of frontiers, either orally, in writing or in print, in the form of art, or\nthrough any other media of his choice.\n3.\nThe exercise of the rights provided for in paragraph 2 of this article\ncarries with it special duties and responsibilities. It may therefore be subject to\n\nInternational Covenant on Civil and Political Rights  Schedule 2\n\nAustralian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\ncertain restrictions, but these shall only be such as are provided by law and are\nnecessary:\n(a) For respect of the rights or reputations of others;\n(b) For the protection of national security or of public order (ordre\npublic), or of public health or morals.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-19-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-19-logic-deontic-1"
        },
