    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-44",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44 International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights  Schedule 2",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-44"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986.pdf, p.148",
      "values:originalText": "Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nThe provisions for the implementation of the present Covenant shall apply\nwithout prejudice to the procedures prescribed in the field of human rights by or\nunder the constituent instruments and the conventions of the United Nations and\nof the specialized agencies and shall not prevent the States Parties to the present\nCovenant from having recourse to other procedures for settling a dispute in\naccordance with general or special international agreements in force between\nthem.",
      "skos:definition": "Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nThe provisions for the implementation of the present Covenant shall apply\nwithout prejudice to the procedures prescribed in the field of human rights by or\nunder the constituent instruments and the conventions of the United Nations and\nof the specialized agencies and shall not prevent the States Parties to the present\nCovenant from having recourse to other procedures for settling a dispute in\naccordance with general or special international agreements in force between\nthem.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986-article-44-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cc82c09dc43895a720ed5fc76299c328eecd2a86043706f12f005fcaec205ef5",
      "skos:note": "States Parties can use other procedures for settling disputes."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986#article-44",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44 International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights  Schedule 2",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 148,
      "values:originalText": "Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nThe provisions for the implementation of the present Covenant shall apply\nwithout prejudice to the procedures prescribed in the field of human rights by or\nunder the constituent instruments and the conventions of the United Nations and\nof the specialized agencies and shall not prevent the States Parties to the present\nCovenant from having recourse to other procedures for settling a dispute in\naccordance with general or special international agreements in force between\nthem."
    },
